{"coverage_basis":"not_exhaustively_mapped","status":"unknown"}},"claim_text_sha256":"326d51ef014be986e79fecc1a31b574cf10badb63dcf1dfa49d95f0d31dfc12f","evidence":{"authority_availability":"available","authority_receipt_ref":"receipts/acceptance/first_wave/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit_fixture_acceptance.json","evidence_class":"external_subprocess_witness","fresh_run_status":"not_run_by_index","historical_receipt_refs":["receipts/first_wave/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit_result.json","receipts/first_wave/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit_board.json","receipts/first_wave/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit_validation_receipt.json","receipts/acceptance/first_wave/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit_fixture_acceptance.json"],"receipt_time_basis":"historical_saved_artifact"},"formal_subclaim_ids":[],"primary_guide_id":"paper_module.agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit","primary_guide_ref":"paper_modules/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit.md","registered_runner_ref":"src/microcosm_core/organs/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit.py","replay_id":"replay::agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit","requirements_review":{"status":"unrecorded"},"summary":"Checks fixture commit, ledger and test claims using a temporary Git repository and a pytest subprocess.","title":"Audit claims about a completed task"},"claim_ceiling":"tool witness only, not general proof authority","claim_ceiling_restated":"Checks the fixture's commit, ledger and test claims by inspecting a temporary Git copy and running the named pytest test, rejecting a fake commit, ledger or test claim and a pass that was never checked.","claim_id":"claim::agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit","evidence_class":"external_subprocess_witness","evidence_strength_rank":4,"organ_id":"agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit","truth_accounting_bucket":"real_runtime_receipt","validator_command":"python -m microcosm_core.organs.agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit run --input fixtures/first_wave/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit/input --out receipts/first_wave/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit --acceptance-out receipts/acceptance/first_wave/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit_fixture_acceptance.json"},"claim_clause_coverage":{"claim_text_sha256":"493938fca0289f7724ee64e973c33a96849df47b7f689b91fd6463acfd9c4365","clauses":[],"mapped_clause_count":null,"status":"unknown","whole_claim_coverage":"unknown"},"classification":{"evidence_class":"external_subprocess_witness","family":"agent_reliability_and_safety","real_substrate_disposition":"real_substrate_capsule","truth_accounting_bucket":"real_runtime_receipt"},"component_id":"agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit","evidence_state":{"current_backend_binding":{"status":"not_checked"},"fresh_prover":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"fresh_replay":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"index_state":"retained_generated_snapshot"},"guide":{"availability":"available","guide_id":"paper_module.agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit","plain":"An automated assistant's closing report may say it saved its work and passed a test when it did not. This component is given claims in a fixed format about a saved snapshot, a log entry and a test, plus a small example project. It compares the claimed snapshot and log entry with the project's records, runs the named test, and accepts a pass claim only if the test succeeded and the claim says the result was checked. The output lists which claims held up and whether the test passed, so a reader can compare a closing report with what happened.","plain_availability":"available","ref":"paper_modules/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit.md","sha256":"dc756af8b4b3757cff4a05dc73898b1e61a41ef3bf236cdc525b9cdf06a8a20a","text":"# Audit claims about a completed task\n\n> **In plain terms.** An automated assistant's closing report may say it saved its work and passed a test when it did not. This component is given claims in a fixed format about a saved snapshot, a log entry and a test, plus a small example project. It compares the claimed snapshot and log entry with the project's records, runs the named test, and accepts a pass claim only if the test succeeded and the claim says the result was checked. The output lists which claims held up and whether the test passed, so a reader can compare a closing report with what happened.\n\nThis audit checks structured claims about a commit, a ledger entry and a test against a public fixture. It copies the fixture repository into a temporary directory, uses Git to create and inspect its HEAD, and runs the named pytest test. A test-pass claim needs both a zero exit status and an explicit indication that the status was checked. The ledger claim is checked against the supplied fixture ledger.\n\nFor example, a commit reference that does not match the temporary repository HEAD is rejected. A missing pytest node or an unchecked pass claim is also rejected. The audit evaluates structured fixture claims; it does not read arbitrary closeout prose or verify a real project’s ledger or deployment.\n\nThe example requires Git and a Python interpreter with pytest available; install the repository’s test dependencies with `python3 -m pip install -e '.[test]'` if needed. The runner probes for a pytest-capable interpreter and blocks the pytest lane if none is available.\n\n## Run the example\n\nFrom the repository root, with Python 3.11 or newer and the repository dependencies available:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=src python3 -m microcosm_core.organs.agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit \\\n  run --input fixtures/first_wave/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit/input \\\n  --out .microcosm/component-guides/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit/output \\\n  --acceptance-out .microcosm/component-guides/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit/acceptance.json\n```\n\nThe result records which claims were verified and whether the pytest span ran and passed. It is written under `.microcosm/component-guides/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit/output`; the acceptance receipt is separate. These paths do not overwrite the checked-in receipts.\n\n## Verification\n\nTests and fixtures exercise the commit, ledger and subprocess checks; they do not formally prove the closeout audit algorithm. The command above runs directly, without the shared admission gate. `make component-replays` separately runs the exported closeout bundle through the [Dafny-verified admission decision](../formal/replay/README.md), checking the host's observations of source and input identities, claim policy and receipt agreement.\n\n## Source\n\n[Implementation](../src/microcosm_core/organs/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit.py) · [fixture input](../fixtures/first_wave/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit/input/) · [tests](../tests/test_agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit.py) · [sample result (historical)](../receipts/first_wave/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit_result.json) · [JSON record](agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit.json).\n\n[FEVER](https://arxiv.org/abs/1803.05355) is related work on evidence-backed claims.\n"},"proofs":[],"replay":{"command":"make component-replays","command_ref":"scripts/check/check_component_replays.py","command_scope":"all registered components","configuration_refs":["src/microcosm_core/runtime_shell.py#RUNTIME_STEPS","src/microcosm_core/runtime_shell.py#_accepted_organ_runner_module_refs"],"declared_prerequisites":{"availability_status":"not_assessed_by_index","description":"Lean, Swift and test extras required","source_ref":"Makefile"},"execution_status":"not_run_by_index","fresh_receipt_template":".microcosm/component-replays/<run>/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit/exported_agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit_bundle_validation_result.json","guide_example":{"command":"microcosm agent-closeout-faithfulness-audit run --input fixtures/first_wave/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit/input --out receipts/first_wave/agent_closeout_faithfulness_audit","expected_result_descriptio